      "message": "This is still v6, so there\u0027s still the fallback when programming a keyslot fails:\n\n        /* Get device keyslot if supported */\n        if (keyslot_manager_crypto_mode_supported(q-\u003eksm,\n                                                  bc-\u003ebc_key-\u003ecrypto_mode,\n                                                  bc-\u003ebc_key-\u003edata_unit_size,\n                                                  bc-\u003ebc_key-\u003eis_hw_wrapped)) {\n                err \u003d bio_crypt_ctx_acquire_keyslot(bc, q-\u003eksm);\n                if (!err)\n                        return 0;\n\n                pr_warn_once(\"Failed to acquire keyslot for %s (err\u003d%d).  Falling back to crypto API.\\n\",\n                             bio-\u003ebi_disk-\u003edisk_name, err);\n        }\n\n        /* Fallback to crypto API */\n        err \u003d blk_crypto_fallback_submit_bio(bio_ptr);\n        if (err)\n                goto out;\n\nSo, it\u0027s theoretically possible to get into blk-crypto-fallback with a wrapped key.\n\nBut for v9 it did look like the checks here were unnecessary and could be removed.",
